module gunbc.joint_claim_join_seed_growth

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.types { String }
import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }

// Seed-growth obligation for the joint-claim join instrument, checkpoint 1 of
// gunbc.plans.joint_incompatibility_claim_join. Homed here, beside the obligation it declares,
// rather than in gunbc.seed_growth_admission, which owns the roster and the join.
//
// WHAT THE CHANGE IS. One cargo bin, v1_compiler.bin.joint_claim_join, that computes for each change
// the two set differences a joint-incompatibility question needs -- export-surface entries removed
// (declared, variants, reexported; base minus head) and import-member claims added or retired -- and
// intersects them across a set of changes, excluding a claim no longer live when the entry left. It
// reuses the parse the wave wall already performs (namespace_wave_admission base_records over
// declaration_index record_from_module) and the diff listing it already trusts (diff_sides); it adds
// no parse, no phase, no job and no permission. Retrospective mode walks a first-parent commit range.
//
// THE EXHIBITED COST, which is what admits this under the v1 PURPOSE test rather than either DESIGN
// trigger: three main reds on 2026-09-10, about an hour each, of a class no check compiles -- two
// individually green, textually disjoint PRs whose union does not compile. The manager's ruling on
// the scope (2026-09-11) was that the raw-candidates-to-findings figure that decides the mitigation is worth acting on
// only if it has an entry point behind it (DESIGN section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe
// its output). This bin is that entry point. It is an instrument that serves the self-host program
// the same way v1_src_dag_parse does: it measures the corpus the program compiles, and its output is
// read by nothing that gates.
//
// CLASSIFIED AGAINST THE FIVE REFUSED CLASSES. NewLanguageBehavior: no -- the compile pipeline is
// byte-untouched. NewCompatibilityObligation: no. NewEscapeHatchOrAdmissionRow: no -- nothing skips
// anything; the bin is not on the required path. SeedFeatureCompletion: no -- the seed compiler gains
// no capability. PublicSurfaceGrowth: no -- a bin contributes no pub mod line to the emitted lib.rs;
// what grows is the SeedRetained roster, enumerated here in full.
//
// NO UNCITABLE ITEM. The one method the first draft carried (a key() on ImportClaimSite) was made a
// free function before this row was written, so every item is nameable as a WholeDeclaration
// DeclarationRef; test-module items are enumerated under the tests submodule path.
//
// RUNG, HONESTLY. The class this instrument measures stays at its ceiling record's rung
// (gunbc.plans.ci_merge_freshness; gunbc.merge_admission receipt_is_admissible, deferred). This bin
// establishes no rung for it: it is executed by nobody on the merge path, and its own evidence is
// the fixture-boundary controls in its tests module -- one positive control per instance shape and
// one discriminating RED for the exclusion -- which run under cargo test, itself off the merge path.

